    "imageAlt": "",
    "bio": "Hajime Satō is a Japanese film and television director and screenwriter born in 1929. He became known for genre filmmaking during the 1960s. His credits include the superhero adventure The Golden Bat and the science-fiction series Captain Ultra. Satō also directed House of Terrors, an atmospheric black-and-white horror film. His best-known work internationally is Goke, Body Snatcher from Hell, which combines alien invasion, social conflict, and vivid visual effects. His films helped define the eccentric science-fiction and horror output produced by Japanese studios during that era.",
